config DISPLAY_WAVESHARE_ESP32S3_RGB
	bool "Waveshare ESP32-S3 LCD_CAM RGB/DPI display driver (experimental, out-of-tree)"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_WAVESHARE_ESP32S3_LCD_CAM_RGB_ENABLED
	select DISPLAY
	help
	  Experimental out-of-tree driver that programs the ESP32-S3 LCD_CAM
	  peripheral in parallel RGB/DPI timing-generator mode plus a
	  dedicated GDMA channel driven directly at the HAL level (bypassing
	  Zephyr's generic espressif,esp32-gdma driver, which does not support
	  cyclic/circular descriptor lists needed for continuous frame
	  streaming). Unblank resets the LCD and DMA and primes the FIFO
	  before starting pixel output. Applications can blank the display
	  while drawing their initial frame to avoid concurrent PSRAM
	  rendering and scanout during startup. Hardware validation is
	  still required. The pixel clock uses the Espressif HAL divider
	  calculation, including its prescaler workaround for LCD clock
	  instability when the pixel-clock prescaler is bypassed.
	  Two internal-SRAM bounce buffers isolate GDMA from PSRAM bus
	  contention. An IRAM-resident VSYNC handler recovers missed buffer
	  deadlines, compensating for the ESP32-S3 LCD FIFO's retained pixels.
	  PSRAM/cache must remain accessible while scanout is active; blank
	  the display before operations that disable external-memory access.
